<in-rbi-rep:BriefHistory contextRef='fromto_20260414_20260415_1'>Branch has sanctioned housing loan of Rs.32.00 lakh on 11.10.2013 for purchase of flat to Mr. Alok Kumar Das &amp; Mrs. Sarmistha Mondal.   Panel Advocate, Mr. Surya Narayan Mohanty had given LSR without verifying the sharing agreement for allocation of flat between Builder/developers &amp; land owner, at the time of sanction of the loan.   Bank executed tripartite agreement between borrower and builder/developer (M/s. Basera Designs Pvt Ltd.) on 11.10.2013 for purchase of flat no. 202, 2nd floor, Basera Impression Plus, Patia, Bhubaneswar.   However, as per available records, no registered sale deed was executed by the builder in favour of Mr. Devi Prasad Pattanaik and Mrs. Sanjukta Jena. Therefore, they did not acquire absolute ownership or legal title over the said flat.      The said Flat no. 202 is not registered in the name of the borrowers as it is already allotted to Smt. Gayatri Kanungo as reported by them vide letter dated 21.10.2017 as per which they are having the possession over it.   Thereafter, accounts turned NPA on 29.01.2018.   Later, bank has taken fresh LSR from advocate Mr. Radhamadhab Mohanty on 09.03.2021, which stated that Mr. Alok Kumar Das, has no valid clear and marketable title to the property for the sake of creation of equitable mortgage.                                               Investigation done by Mr. B K Swain, Chief Manager, Bhubhaneshwar Region on 27.05.2024. Details of report are as under:   Builder/Promoters M/s Basera Designs Pvt Ltd. represented through its Managing director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik has allotted the same flat i.e. Flat No.202, to two different persons i.e. Mr. Alok Kumar Das (our Borrower) as well land owner Mrs. Gayatri Kanungo vide allotment letter dated 20.09.2013 &amp; 10.03.2012 respectively. However, it has been reported by the branch to Regional office, Bhubaneswar vide letter dated 23.10.2017 that branch has got some information that said flat No. 202 (financed to Mr. Alok Kumar Das) has been registered in favour of another borrower i.e. Mr. Subrat Kumar Das S/o Swapneswar Das (our borrower for flat no. 101 &amp; 004) but no documentary evident found on record.    Builder/ Promoters M/s Basera Designs Pvt Ltd. represented through its Managing Director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik has fraudulently allotted the same flat to more than one person without the knowledge of Bank.     Builder/ Promoters M/s Basera Designs Pvt Ltd. represented through its Managing Director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik has breached the terms of tripartite agreement.    Advocate Mr. Suryanarayan Mohanty vide his LSR dated 01.10.2013 has given the report without verifying the sharing agreement for allocation of flat between Builder/ Developers &amp; land owner. Without verification of the sharing agreement for allocation of flat, the authority to execute the sale agreement for particular flat could not be ascertained and without ascertaining the same advocate has given his LSR. Thus he opined that LSR given by the advocate is not complete to decide the ownership over the particular flat.    Based on the advocate&apos;s report and also without ascertaining the fact that who is the actual owner of the particular flat, Branch has financed the said flat considering M/s Basera Designs Pvt Ltd. represented through its Managing Director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik (i.e. executer of sale agreement) as actual owner.     Branch has not done proper due diligence about the Promoters /builder before sanction of the loan. Had the Branch taken due care about mapping of flat (i.e. allocation/sharing of flat between developer/Builders &amp; land owners) interest of bank would have been protected. Based on the investigation report dated 27.05.2024, SCNs were issued to borrowers and builder.  Later ZO Raipur, advised to conduct a fresh investigation which was allotted to Mr. Sarat Chandra Mohapatra, CM, Regional Office Bhubaneshwar. The details of the report dated 06.05.2025 are as under:-   Builder/developers M/S Basera Designs Pvt. Ltd, represented through its Managing Director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik has allotted the flat No-202 fraudulently to Mr. Alok Kumar Das (our borrower) which was revealed once Mrs. Gayatri Kanungo produced a letter dated 21.10.2017, claiming her to be the actual owner of the said flat No-202.   The fraudulent allotment of flat by Managing Director of M/S Basera Designs Pvt. Ltd to our borrower Mr. Alok Kumar Das, but the borrower has also not demanded the execution of sale deed to the developer even almost all amount have been paid to the developer by 20.02.2014.   The Promoter has clearly mislead the bank with false agreement for Acquisition of ownership in apartment and tripartite agreement for providing the flats pertaining to owner share in the project and taken away the major portion of consideration amount from bank whom the HBL were sanctioned.   The LSR provided by the advocate Mr. Surya Narayan Mohanty is not clear about the person with whom the tripartite agreement is to be executed. He has also not verified the construction agreement for allocation of flat.   Hence the connivance of our HBL borrowers along with advocate cannot be ignored.   Root cause analysis/Systemic deficiency/Irregularities:                                              The builder has allotted the same flat i.e. Flat No.202, to two different persons i.e. Mr. Alok Kumar Das (our Borrower) as well land owner Mrs. Gayantri Kanungo vide allotment letter dated 20.09.2013 &amp; 10.03.2012 respectively.    Builder/Developer, M/S Basera Designs Pvt. Ltd, represented through Managing Director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik executed Tripartite Agreement with borrower &amp; bank by hiding the fact that the flat was already allotted to land owner Mrs. Gayantri Kanungo vide allotment letter dated 10.03.2012.   Even though the loan amount was disbursed to the developer by 20.02.2014, the Borrowers not even enquired about the execution of Sale deed with builder, which clearly shows the connivance of the borrower with the builder.   Panel Advocate/ Branch failed to ascertain owner of the flat No. 202 and relied on the false agreement entered between builder/developer and purchaser. Later on, it was transpired that the subject flat no. 202 was in the share of part land owner.  Show Cause Notices issued to Borrower, Co-Borrower and Builder on 06.07.2024 &amp; 10.09.2024. Borrower and co-borrower submit their reply/representation against our SCN on 16.09.2024. Their after Branch has given rebuttal reply to them on 15.10.2024.  After issuing of SCN their is no reply/representation received from Builder.</in-rbi-rep:BriefHistory>
<in-rbi-rep:ModusOperandi contextRef='fromto_20260414_20260415_1'>Builder/Promoters M/s Basera Designs Pvt Ltd. represented through its Managing director Mr. Manoj Kumar Pattnaik has allotted the same flat i.e. Flat No.202, to two different persons i.e. Mr. Alok Kumar Das (our Borrower) as well land owners Mrs. Gayatri Kanungo vide allotment letter dated 20.09.2013 &amp; 10.03.2012 respectively.    The housing loan was sanctioned to Mr. Alok Kumar Das &amp; Mrs. Sarmistha Mondal on 11.10.2013 for purchase of flat no. 202, 2nd floor in Basera Impression Plus, Patia, Bhubaneswar, on the basis of false allotment letter.   Neither registration done in favour of borrower nor EM created.</in-rbi-rep:ModusOperandi>
